- op: discuss  # 27b0
  at: '2026-09-24T22:31:22Z'  # 27b0
  by: agent  # 27b0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 27b0
  clock: 3  # 27b0
  nonce: 27b0  # 27b0
  message: "Fixed in PR #1191 (c99539ad34). The row's three asks:\n\n1. ENUMERATED. An audit hook (sitecustomize on PYTHONPATH, so the scripts a test runs as subprocesses were traced too) logged every non-Python file under packages/*/src/*/<dir>/ opened during the whole root suite (1973 passed). 13 root test files open catalogue data. The existing term grep selected 0 of them. They are: test_measure_catalogue_exposure (io_primitives, through the script), test_generate_concepts (frameworks, through scripts/generate-concepts), test_bakeoff_deep_integration, test_ci_failover_retired, test_measure_taint_precision, test_rct_public_api_pinned, test_tracker_json_flag_documented, test_adr_readme_index_sync, test_agent_supervisor_meta_breaker, and four test_auto*_ files. Most of these load the data incidentally, through the CLI or an import. Table: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/juzoz_09242026/selection_before.txt.\n\n2. ROUTE. The option taken is over-selection. A second hop (terms -> the scripts that name them, comments stripped -> the root tests that name those scripts) was measured and reached only 4 of the 13. So when the catalogue gate fires, smart-test now unions the whole root suite: 1973 tests, 78 s locally.\n\n3. MUTATION CHECK, end to end. I ran `smart-test --manifest` in two worktrees, with #1162's java.yaml diff as the only change (BASE_BRANCH=HEAD). Without the fix (dev 99281e3c43): 166 test files selected; the exposure test was NOT among them; 7 of 116 root tests. With the fix: 275 selected; the exposure test was selected; all 116 root tests. The new tests in tests/test_smart_test.py (TestCatalogueSelectsTheRootSuite) run the script's own catalogue block. Two of them went red before the fix, for the expected reason.\n\nScope NOT asserted: the tracer sees files opened by Python processes only. A root test that reads catalogue data only from a shell pipeline would not have appeared in the enumeration. The union covers it anyway."  # 27b0
